<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sharaf al-Din Ali Yazdi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1454</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sharaf al-Din Ali Yazdi was a Persian historian and poet of the Timurid court, born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yazd">Yazd</a>. His <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zafarnama">Zafarnama</a> ('Book of Victory'), completed around 1425 for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shah-rukh">Shah Rukh</a>'s son Ibrahim <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a>, is a polished panegyric history of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timur">Timur</a>'s life and conquests. It became the standard account of Timur in the Persian world and was later richly illustrated at Timurid and Mughal courts.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sharaf-al-din-ali-yazdi.jpg" alt="Sharaf al-Din Ali Yazdi" width="320" height="490" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: British Library · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sharaf_al-Din_%27Ali_Yazdi_(d.1454)_with_Muhammad_Amuli_for_whom_he_wrote_poems_and_riddles,_Majalis_al-%27ushshaq,_Shiraz,_Iran,_c.1560.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
